<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SMS_Westfalen" title=3D"SMS =
Westfalen">SMS&nbsp;<i>Westfalen</i></a></b> was a <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Nassau-class_battleship" title=3D"Nassau-class battleship"=
><i>Nassau</i>-class dreadnought battleship</a> built for the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_German_Navy" title=3D"Imperial German =
Navy">Imperial German Navy</a>. <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ke=
el_laying" title=3D"Keel laying">Laid down</a> in 1907 and launched in July=
 1908, she was commissioned into the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/High_Seas_Fleet" title=3D"High Seas Fleet">High Seas Fleet</a> in Novemb=
er&nbsp;1909. She was equipped with a main battery of twelve 28&nbsp;cm (11=
&nbsp;in) guns in six twin <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun_tur=
ret" title=3D"Gun turret">turrets</a> using an unusual hexagonal arrangemen=
t <i>(pictured)</i>. <i>Westfalen</i> saw extensive service in the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sea" title=3D"North Sea">North Sea<=
/a> in the early years of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wa=
r_I" title=3D"World War I">World War&nbsp;I</a>. In the early hours of 1&nb=
sp;June 1916, she was heavily engaged in fighting against British light for=
ces during the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Jutland" =
title=3D"Battle of Jutland">Battle of Jutland</a>, severely damaging severa=
l British <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroyer" title=3D"Dest=
royer">destroyers</a>. On another fleet sortie in August&nbsp;1916, she was=
 damaged by a torpedo from a British <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Submarine" title=3D"Submarine">submarine</a>. Later in the war, <i>Westf=
alen</i> participated in sorties into the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Baltic_Sea" title=3D"Baltic Sea">Baltic Sea</a> against the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Navy" title=3D"Russian Navy">Russ=
ian Navy</a>, and to support the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W=
hite_Guard_(Finland)" title=3D"White Guard (Finland)">White Finns</a> in th=
e <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_Civil_War" title=3D"Finn=
ish Civil War">Finnish Civil War</a>. She was ceded to the Allies after the=
 war and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_breaking" title=3D"S=
hip breaking">broken up</a> in 1924. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/SMS_Westfalen" title=3D"SMS Westfalen">This&nbsp;article</a></b> =
is part of a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Featured_to=
pics" title=3D"Wikipedia:Featured topics">featured topic</a>: <b><a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Featured_topics/Battleships_of_Ger=
many" title=3D"Wikipedia:Featured topics/Battleships of Germany"><i>Battles=
hips of Germany</i></a></b>.)</i>
</p>
